  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "In science club, Hana tried an experiment with two paper bridges.",
      "She folded one sheet into a flat shape and another into a narrow strip.",
      "Then she placed coins on each bridge until it fell."
    ],
    [
      "The narrow bridge held more coins.",
      "Hana called it the better design and began writing her report.",
      "However, her partner noticed that she had used thicker paper for that bridge."
    ],
    [
      "Their approach had changed two things at once: the shape and the paper.",
      "The result was evidence of what happened in that test, but not enough to explain which change mattered.",
      "They needed another test."
    ],
    [
      "As an alternative, they made both bridges from the same type of paper.",
      "They also kept the gap between the books the same.",
      "This time, they repeated each test before comparing the results.",
      "Hana changed her report: one successful attempt was a useful beginning, not the end of the investigation."
    ]
  ],
  "translations": [
    "在科学社团里，哈娜用两座纸桥做了一个实验。",
    "她把一张纸折成平坦的形状，把另一张折成较窄的纸条。",
    "然后，她往每座桥上放硬币，直到桥倒下。",
    "较窄的桥承受了更多硬币。",
    "哈娜把它称为更好的设计，开始写报告。",
    "然而，搭档注意到，她给那座桥用了更厚的纸。",
    "她们的方法同时改变了两件事：形状和纸张。",
    "结果是那次测试中所发生情况的证据，但不足以解释是哪种变化起了作用。",
    "她们需要再做一次测试。",
    "作为另一种方案，她们用同一种纸制作了两座桥。",
    "她们也让两本书之间的间距保持一致。",
    "这一次，她们重复每项测试后才比较结果。",
    "哈娜修改了报告：一次成功的尝试是有用的开始，而不是探究的终点。"
  ],
